{"resourceIdentifier":"4745","resourceName":"Henan CP Group Swine Farm Biogas Recovery and Utilization Project","description":"Henan CP Group Swine Farm Biogas Recovery and Utilization Project (hereinafter referred to as the project) installs animal waste management systems (AWMSs) to treat the manure from 5 swine farms in Henan Province, China. Each swine farm is to build anaerobic animal manure treatment systems to treat manure waste of Breeding Swine Farms separately in Luoyang, Shangqiu, and Pingdingshan owned and implemented by subsidiaries of Charoen Pokphand Group (CP Group). The purpose of the project activity is to treat the manure and wastewater on site to avoid methane emissions generated in the baseline uncovered anaerobic lagoons.\r\nAll the manure and wastewater are collected and is flushed and pumped to the aerobic treatment system (HDPE Membrane Enclosed Anaerobic Digester). The biogas generated during the treatment process will be captured for heat generation and food processing facility for self-use. An emergency flare is installed in each project activity instance to ensure that biogas would be destroyed when exigencies happened. After anaerobic digestion, the digestate is sent out and used for agriculture fertilization aerobically in the nearby farmlands for free. The effluent will be used for agricultural irrigation. \r\nThe project is expected to avoid GHG emission of methane through recovery and destruction of biogas. It is estimated that 22,432tCO2e emission reductions will be generated annually and total emission reductions are 224,320tCO2e in the 10 years’ fixing crediting period.","location":{"latitude":33.700082,"longitude":112.806055},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2023-11-21","endExclusive":"2023-12-22","endInclusive":"2023-12-21"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"4745"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAM